`F = closure(q^{-1}(C)-H)` is the *other* branch, and it crosses `H` transversally
precisely because the node is transverse.

**(N2) Lemma 5.1(a), via Lemma 5.2.** 3.27's second half invokes Lemma 5.2 to show
