codex
Both advertised countermodels survive an independent computation. The two-conic example is especially decisive: its projective group is \(\langle a,b\mid(ab)^2=1\rangle\cong\mathbb Z*(\mathbb Z/2)\), matching an independent braid-monodromy calculation in Amram–Garber–Teicher, Proposition 3.6. It proves the coefficient \(1\) on cross-component tangency is genuinely sharp, not merely an artifact of the blow-up proof.
