The residual arithmetic is clean: the gate is exactly \(M_\infty+2T\le 3d-3\), and the \((6,3)\) table has no hidden parity condition. The only numerical survivors are indeed \((7,4)\) and \((8,3)\). I’m now narrowing the deformation claims: the conic family refutes universal \(\delta\)-constant \(\pi_1\)-transport, but because it is reducible and projective it does not refute a theorem specially proved for the residual irreducible one-place family. That restricted transport remains open.
